{"name":"Charlie Brown","hex":"#995500","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"charlie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Charlie of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Charlie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charlie"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charlie Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Charles \"Charlie\" Brown is a fictional character and the principal protagonist of the American comic strip Peanuts, created by Charles M. Schulz and syndicated in daily and Sunday newspapers in numerous countries worldwide. Depicted as a \"lovable loser\", Charlie Brown is a popular and widely recognized cartoon character. Charlie Brown is characterized as a person who frequently suffers, and as a result, is usually nervous and lacks self-confidence. He shows both pessimistic and optimistic attitudes: on some days, he is apprehensive to even get out of bed because he cannot face the world, but on others, he hopes to accomplish things and is determined to do his best. Charlie Brown is easily recognized by his round head and trademark zigzag patterned shirt. His catchphrase is \"Good grief\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Charlie_Brown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Brown"},{"title":"Charlie Brown (Coldplay song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Charlie Brown\" is a song by British rock band Coldplay. The song was released as the third single from their fifth studio album Mylo Xyloto. The single was listed by Q magazine as their track of the day on 2 December 2011. The music video for the song was released on 3 February 2012, as well as a live version on 6 December 2011. Despite the name, the lyrics have no relation to the Peanuts franchise."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cb/Coldplay_Charlie_Brown.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Brown_(Coldplay_song)"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/CB1948.jpg/500px-CB1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/CB1948.jpg/500px-CB1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First appearance of a \"Charlie Brown\" from the May 30, 1948 strip of Li'l Folks.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACB1948.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Apollo_10_command_module.jpg/500px-Apollo_10_command_module.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Apollo_10_command_module.jpg/500px-Apollo_10_command_module.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Command Module of Apollo 10 which was named after Charlie Brown","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApollo_10_command_module.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi